1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
You can build a protocol with people you have never met.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
But when it is time to build a company, where do you start?

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Meet Dstruct.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,400
For a web3 founder, incorporation is only the beginning.

5
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,800
Who owns the code?

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,200
Who can sign a contract?

7
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:18,600
How does a shared treasury fit into the business?

8
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:21,000
The questions arrive together.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Imagine two founders, based in France and India, building on Ethereum.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
They use a multisig treasury and want to raise funding.

11
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Their first question is simple: should we form a Delaware company?

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,500
Dstruct would use AI to turn that first message into a focused conversation.

13
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:38,000
Where does the team work?

14
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,500
Who owns the intellectual property?

15
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:43,000
What does the product actually do?

16
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,500
Are tokens part of the plan?

17
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,000
Each answer shapes the next question.

18
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,500
The web3 angle is the relationship between people, legal entities, and onchain activity.

19
00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:03,000
The workspace would bring governance and treasury context into the same review, so advisers can examine wallet control alongside ownership and authority to act for the company.

20
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:10,000
AI would organize the facts into an incorporation brief, highlight open decisions, and suggest the next tasks.

21
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,000
The founder could see what is known, what still needs an answer, and which decisions need specialist review.

22
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,333
A specialist would receive a concise brief with supporting references.

23
00:01:21,333 --> 00:01:25,667
Entity choice, tax exposure, and token plans remain decisions for qualified advisers.

24
00:01:25,667 --> 00:01:30,000
Their review would turn scattered questions into an agreed path forward.

25
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,333
The product vision keeps the working legal file private.

26
00:01:34,333 --> 00:01:38,667
Founders would choose the information they share with each adviser.

27
00:01:38,667 --> 00:01:43,000
Public wallet activity can provide context, while sensitive documents stay in the private workspace.

28
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:49,500
Once the path is agreed, the workspace would track the next steps, from ownership documents to company setup and ongoing obligations.

29
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:56,000
Everyone could see who owns a task and what needs attention before the next milestone.

30
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Our working prototype explores the intake and handoff: five synthetic founder cases, linked official sources, structured questions, and exportable briefs.

31
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:08,000
This walkthrough shows how that foundation could grow into a workspace for web3 founders.

32
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Dstruct.

33
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
An AI workspace to help web3 founders prepare, coordinate, and move their legal work forward.
